Author: CusDeb OS Team
Description: explorer: Use high-DPI Start menu banners and fit the start button to its image.
 The Start menu banner bitmap only exists for 96 DPI. Add banners for
 higher DPIs, rendered from media/graphics/start_menu_banner.svg by
 tools/render_artwork.py into CDEX_ARTWORK_DIR, which the CDEX Makefile
 sets. Their resource identifiers are IDB_STARTMENU_DPI(dpi); the banner
 of the highest DPI up to the screen DPI is loaded and scaled to the
 screen DPI if it differs, by pixel replication for a whole factor and
 with filtering otherwise. The Start menu takes its banner width from the
 bitmap, so the menu layout follows.
 .
 The start button is kept at least as wide as its theme image, which
 grows with the DPI, or the image is squeezed into it.
